<title>CANADA: Ivaco to spend C$13 million on wire mills.</title>
<headline>Ivaco to spend C$13 million on wire mills.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ivaco Inc said it intends to spend C$13 million to expand production facilities at four of its wire mills in Canada and the U.S.</p>
<p>Ivaco said it will install new high speed wire drawing equipment at its Marieville, Quebec plant. The company said it plans to install shot-blasting for cleaning and a new annealing furnaces at its Ingersoll, Ontario plant. In Buffalo, New York a new annealing furnace is being installed and in Newnan, Georgia state-of-the-art acid cleaning and annealing equipment is scheduled for start-up this year.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
